        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "f20088b5bf4aa6878eb1cc459ca16278dfc6861c",
            "parents": [
                "663b7b73184a8687c5c9add63cb58e06d3073f01"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/74/86874/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Patrick Williams",
                "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                "username": "williamspatrick"
            },
            "createdOn": 1769122894,
            "author": {
                "name": "Patrick Williams",
                "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                "username": "williamspatrick"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Overall in support of this.  At one point I had a version of this refactor that turned type_id into a constexpr method with a bunch of std::is_same.  I never finished it because it wasn't clear that was any better than template specialization we had, but it's good to see these get modernized."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm having a bit of trouble getting this all working because it relies on fairly new support.  It seems like GCC 15.2 is the minimum to make it work and Yocto right now is on 15.1.  We'll keep playing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I hit the same.  And took it to a bit of an extreme rewrite of the whole method.  There's probably a middle ground that works.\n\nWorst case, gcc15 isn't too bad to enforce."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/read.hpp",
                    "line": 266,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This couldn't be constexpr anymore?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/read.hpp",
                    "line": 266,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Correct.  Anytime the string potentially lives outside the pure constexpr evaluation state it needs to be converted from a constexpr to a static const.  This is because of small-string-optimization (SSO) and constexpr requirements.\n\nIf the string is long enough to no longer fit into SSO, it would have an allocation.  If this variable were a constexpr, the compiler considers that allocation as having lived past the constexpr-context, and fails the compile.  But, if the string is converted to a static const, it's ok...\n\nYou'll see in this commit a change in the test cases where I had to make a \"ReallyBigType\" to cover this case.  All of the framework code where we potentially hold the type_id, we have to use as a static const to ensure we don't violate the SSO length when leaving the constexpr."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/read.hpp",
                    "line": 266,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Weird.  For some reason I thought constexpr allocators had worked that out, but I guess not."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/types.hpp",
                    "line": 267,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": ".... you can concat and return std::string in constexpr now?  Sweet."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/utility/container_traits.hpp",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not that worried about it, but is there a reason we can't just use is_enum_v directly?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/utility/container_traits.hpp",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "No.  When you use it as a template restriction, you have to use a constraint (ie. a concept).  Here is the compile error with the proposed change:\n\n```\n../include/sdbusplus/message/types.hpp:209:11: error: \u2018std::is_enum_v\u2019 is not a type\n  209 | template <std::is_enum_v T>\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/utility/container_traits.hpp",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "ACK.  makes sense."
                }
            ],
